    "doi": "https://doi.org/10.22271/27889289.2026.v6.i4a.279",
    "abstract": "This study presents a comprehensive analysis of rainfall patterns in the Sindhudurg district utilizing pivot table methodologies. By leveraging detailed rainfall data spanning several years, we aim to identify significant trends and anomalies in precipitation, crucial for agricultural planning, water resource management, and climate adaptation strategies. The dataset, comprising daily rainfall records, is aggregated and analysed to uncover monthly and annual rainfall variations, seasonal distribution, and spatial disparities within the district. The pivot table allows for a multifaceted exploration of the data, facilitating the identification of extreme weather events and long-term shifts in precipitation patterns. Our findings highlight the utility of pivot tables in simplifying complex datasets, offering valuable insights for policymakers, researchers, and local stakeholders invested in sustainable development and climate resilience in Sindhudurg.",
    "field": "Rainfall pattern analysis",
    "problem": "Analyzing large, complex climatological datasets to understand increasingly variable and unpredictable rainfall patterns is challenging, necessitating efficient analytical tools for summarizing multidimensional information and identifying crucial trends for resource management.",
    "method": "This study proposes a method using pivot tables to analyze historical rainfall data to identify temporal, seasonal, and spatial patterns for improved agricultural and water resource management in Sindhudurg district.",
    "task": "The task is to analyze rainfall patterns in the Sindhudurg district using pivot table methodologies to identify trends, variations, and anomalies for agricultural planning and water resource management.",
